This is a Java Spring Boot MVC application.

Architecture rules:
- Use Java and Maven.
- Use WAR packaging because the project uses JSP.
- Use Spring MVC, JSP, and JSTL.
- Keep JSP files under src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/views/.
- Use Spring Data Redis and StringRedisTemplate.
- Use constructor injection only.
- Do not use field injection.
- Keep controllers thin.
- Put business logic in services.
- Put request and response contracts in DTOs.
- Validate all external input.
- Accept only http and https URLs.
- Do not store IP addresses or sensitive visitor data.
- Do not add a relational database unless explicitly requested.
- Do not add authentication unless explicitly requested.
- Do not add Lombok unless explicitly requested.
- Add or update tests when behavior changes.
- Update README.md when setup commands change.
- Run mvn test after modifying backend logic.
